#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:13
msgid "PublishPress plugin actions."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:26
msgid "Discover Permissions features"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:27
msgid "Read active native modules, supported operations and permission requirements. Discovery does not grant access. Credentials and administrator-level grants are not exposed."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:30
msgid "Permissions settings"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:31
msgid "Read native setting identifiers, exact JSON types, defaults, stored values and revision before patching. Checkbox inputs must be JSON booleans. Omitted options remain unchanged; unknown fields and locked settings are rejected. dry_run validates without saving."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:36
msgid "Permissions post types and taxonomies"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:37
msgid "Read native General-tab filtering choices and locks. Patch explicit {name, enabled} rows with the current revision. Checkbox values must be JSON booleans. Omitted and temporarily unregistered types remain unchanged. Locked controls cannot be changed. dry_run saves nothing."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:48
msgid "Permissions groups and members"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:49
msgid "Manage native custom permission groups. Lists are paginated; reads exclude account passwords and email addresses. Read get-group before updates and supply its revision. Membership actions explicitly add or remove user_ids, preserve other members and existing schedules, and require edit_user for every affected user. Built-in role/metagroups cannot be renamed or joined. dry_run saves nothing."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:53
msgid "Permissions supplemental roles"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:54
msgid "Read supplemental roles for a user, custom group or WordPress role metagroup. Changes are explicit {role, enabled} patches with a current revision; other roles remain unchanged. Direct grants use a discovered native direct_roles name, require promote_users and reject administrator-level capabilities; other grants use a discovered pattern role in base:post:post_type or base:term:taxonomy format; status scopes use base:post:post_type:post_status:status with a native active status. Native object-type permissions apply. Administrator-level capabilities are rejected even for administrator sessions. dry_run saves nothing."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:59
msgid "Permissions for posts and terms"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:60
msgid "Read an agent/object/operation scope and its revision before adding or removing a native permission. source=pp_group with operation=manage and assign_for=item manages native custom-group delegation when Collaboration and Display group permissions are enabled. Group management, membership and deletion capabilities are required, and incoming delegation references must be removed before target-group deletion. source=term uses WordPress term IDs and a taxonomy; post_type selects the affected post type for category-based rules. mod_type is additional, include or exclude; assign_for is item, children or both. Native operation, object and descendant permissions apply. Omitted rules are preserved. Inherited rules must be changed at their origin. dry_run writes nothing. Large scopes use native administration."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:75
msgid "Permissions teaser settings"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:75
msgid "Permissions module activation"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:77
msgid "Read native teaser modes, messages, redirects, RSS and notice styles. Omit post_type for global options; pass a discovered filtered post type for per-type settings. Patch exact native option names with JSON types and revision. Rich text uses native sanitization. Redirect destinations require object permissions. dry_run saves nothing."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:78
msgid "Discover installed, required and active native modules. Patch explicit module/enabled rows with a current revision. Required modules cannot be disabled. Native lifecycle hooks run; activation changes load on the next request. Network changes require network administration. dry_run saves nothing."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:84
msgid "Delete a custom permission group"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:85
msgid "Read get-group-deletion for the full native deletion scope and revision. Only custom groups can be deleted. All members, roles, rules and inherited permission targets are checked before cleanup. dry_run previews without deleting. Unknown or oversized permission scopes require native administration."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:90
msgid "Permissions Role Usage"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:91
msgid "Read native Role Usage choices: 0 (no supplemental assignment), pattern, or direct. Patch discovered roles with a current revision; omitted roles remain unchanged. Administrator-level roles cannot be enabled. Existing assignments must be removed before changing an assigned role interpretation. dry_run saves nothing."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:96
msgid "Permissions content visibility shortcode"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:97
msgid "Discover or build the native pp_restrict shortcode with typed logged-in/out, role, capability, username and group conditions. relation is all or any; hide is a JSON boolean. The builder sanitizes HTML and never saves a post. Use native content-editing tools with object permissions to place its result. Nested visibility shortcodes require native editing."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:102
msgid "Permissions editor and screen controls"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:103
msgid "Read native per-post-type Permissions metabox and Permissions-screen switches, including their exact native option names and stored values. Only the native string 0 disables them; absent and legacy values default enabled. Writes require JSON booleans, the current revision, native settings and post-type capabilities. Omitted controls stay unchanged; dry_run saves nothing."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:108
msgid "Permissions validated batch"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:109
msgid "Supply up to 25 explicit items, each with its own current revision. Every item is validated and authorized before writes; malformed, denied, stale or overlapping permission scopes reject the whole preview. dry_run writes nothing. Native execution is not transactional: inspect completed, confirmed_items and failed_index and re-read all scopes after a partial failure."
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:112
msgid "Read explicit permission scopes"
msgstr ""

#: classes/PublishPress/Permissions/Mcp/Registry.php:113
msgid "Read up to 25 explicit authorized post, term or custom-group delegation scopes with their native rules and individual revisions. This does not enumerate private objects or grant access. Results are bounded to 1,000 rules; use the normal single-scope getters or smaller batches for larger inventories."
msgstr ""

